{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/354396-lifeweb-review-critique","id":354396,"title":"Lifeweb Review/Critique","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-29T20:59:48-08:00","id":354396,"title":"Lifeweb Review/Critique","content":"Okay, so Lifeweb is out. Yay! Nice to see Monitor love. Nice to see anything Wraithly get love after all this time, really. Before I start kvetching, I do want to thank everyone for their hard work on the game; I do appreciate it. So, some complaints/observations/rants:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT\">Tsuchigumo <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">are Lifeweb empowed petty criminals, </span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Should probably be &quot;empowered&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">If the Fetter somehow wound<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"> up in the Underworld, the difficulty is 7 if it's in the Shadowlands, 8 if it's in the Tempest, and 9<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">if it's in the Labyrinth, closest to Oblivion.</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Sentence needs cleaning, but more to the point: Unless the Shroud also has very high difficulties, then those are some very high difficulties for a Fetter in the Underworld. I can see Oblivion jacking up the use of Arcanoi, but reading this it seems like it would be easier to access a Fetter that was across the Shroud in some cases than if it were right next to you in the Shadowlands. That doesn't seem right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Even the subtlest Lifeweb uses can have an observer effect, potentially warning the target that<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">the Monitor is examining him. When a wraith is subject to any Lifeweb art that isn't<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">immediately obvious through other means, he may make a Perception + Awareness roll. One<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">success alerts him to the fact that someone's toying with part of his being; with three or more<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">successes, he identifies the Monitor as the source.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This needs clarity. Can a wraith perceive a Lifeweb art if it is being used on one of her Fetters at a remote location, rather than on herself directly? Assuming she gets three successes, how much information is revealed about the Monitor? If the Monitor is concealed somehow, such as being part of a crowd, behind a curtain, or hiding with a different Arcanoi, will multiple successes reveal his location?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">When the Monitor extends her senses to one of her Fetters, the player rolls Perception + Lifeweb.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Each success on this roll allows her to use one die of her normal Perception + Alertness pool to<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">survey the Fetter's location</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Mathematically, this is gonna be a small dicepool by the end of things. It's also rolling dice to see how many dice you get to roll. I might suggest just making it a pass/fail roll, or making Perception+Lifeweb the roll to look around the location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">If the player spends 1 Pathos when activating this art, she also may assess the Fetter's location<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">with a Perception + Awareness roll, subject to the same dice pool limit</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I cannot readily understand the difference between &quot;surveying&quot; and &quot;assessing&quot; a location. You might want to clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Vibrations in the Web (Ancient)<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">While Sense Strands focuses on the Monitor's own Fetters, this complementary art extends her<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">perceptions outward, enabling her to perceive the connections between other wraiths and their<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Fetters.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT\">System: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">When the Monitor examines another wraith, the player player spends 1 Pathos and rolls<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Perception + Lifeweb. <b>The target may resist with Willpower if he desires.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Does the target need to be aware to resist? It would be weird otherwise. Or is this one of the uses of Lifeweb that is immediately obvious?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The player spends 2 Pathos and rolls Intelligence + Lifeweb. For one turn per success,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">the wraith may use any Arcanos art she knows as if she were at the Fetter's location (though she<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">may still use them normally at her own location if she so chooses). She also may speak through<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">the Fetter, with her voice seeming to originate from it</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Seems kind of expensive for the overall effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">If the wraith isn't already using Sense Strands to perceive her Fetter's location, every two<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">successes on the roll to activate Strand Channel count as one success for Sense Strands. This<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">applies even if the Monitor doesn't know Sense Strands</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>A weird and needless complexity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The character first touches the living being, place, or material object that she wants to<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">make into a temporary Fetter. The player spends 3 Pathos and rolls Intelligence + Lifeweb.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">With any successes, the target becomes a new one-dot Fetter for the Monitor.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">During the same scene, the Monitor may transfer the temporary Fetter from herself to another<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">wraith, whom she must touch. The player spends 1 additional Pathos and rolls Intelligence +<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Lifeweb (difficulty 7). If the subject wraith is unwilling, this becomes a resisted roll against his<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Willpower, and the Monitor's Shadow gains 1 temporary Angst. If the Monitor succeeds, the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">temporary Fetter transfers from her to the target wraith</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Once again we are rolling dice to roll dice. Couldn't we just make it one roll, and just say transferring to another wraith ups the difficulty?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The Monitor may use Splice Strand to repair the effect of Sever Strand. All difficulties increase<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">by 1, but success restores the Fetter at its full strength and permanence (and ongoing Pathos<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">maintenance is unnecessary)</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be harder to reattach something that already had all the prerequisites of being Fetter? I would remove the difficulty increase here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The Monitor must touch the target Fetter. The player spends 2 Pathos and 1 Willpower<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">and makes a resisted Intelligence + Lifeweb roll against the Fetter owner's Willpower. Each net<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">success reduces the Fetter by 1 dot and grants the Monitor's Shadow 1 temporary Angst</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I rolled so well that I wound up in Catharsis? That is potentially a lot of Angst for the effect. A straight Angst cost would be more fair, and more tempting. Something is wrong when the Puppeteer can destroy your wife's soul and get less Angst than I can for just reversibly severing your emotional connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Drawing on the spiritual tug of a Fetter, the Monitor can travel to it with breathtaking speed.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">This allows not only convenient travel for ordinary business but a swift rescue of a threatened<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Fetter. However, a wise Monitor looks before leaping \u2013 threatening a Fetter to lure a wraith into<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">ambush is a time-honored tactic.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT\">System: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The player spends 3 Pathos and 2 Corpus and rolls Perception + Lifeweb. Successes<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">determine travel time, regardless of distance:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">1 success One hour.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">2 successes 15 minutes.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">3 successes One minute.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">4 successes 15 seconds (5 turns).<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">5 successes One turn.<br /> </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\"><br /> <br /> Okay, first of all is the cost. Are you kidding? Three Pathos and two Corpus is not &quot;convenient travel&quot;, it's a punch in the face. So if this cost is kept it's going to be only for dire emergencies. Secondly, and more importantly, this power punishes mild success more than failure. Say some enemy is smashing up your Fetters, and you use this power to stop them. If you fail, one Fetter is smashed, too bad, but you might have time to protect another one. Just get one success, and now not only is your Fetter still broken, but also you're stuck doing nothing for an hour. I would push this time chart down a bit. If your Fetter is genuinely in danger, you likely have turns, not minutes, to do something about it.<br /> <br /> It might even be better to have two versions for travel and for emergencies, with one costing more but being faster, and the other costing less and being slower. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The Monitor must touch the being she wishes to bond as a Fetter. The player spends 5<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Pathos and 3 Willpower and rolls Intelligence + Lifeweb. The number of successes determine<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">the new Fetter's strength:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">1-2 successes Fetter \u2022<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">3-5 successes Fetter \u2022\u2022<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">6+ successes Fetter \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This makes for a pretty weak Fetter for the cost, and has kind of a wonky structure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The Monitor can use this art on a living (or undead) supernatural being, but doing so requires an<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">additional Pathos expenditure equal to the subject's Willpower. The subject also must spend 5<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">points of whatever supernatural energy it uses in lieu of Pathos (e.g., Blood, Rage, Quintessence,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">and if all else fails, Willpower). Using Souls Interwoven on a vampire or other undead creature<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">also gives the Monitor's Shadow an amount of temporary Angst equal to half the deathless thing's<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Willpower</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. </div> </div> </div>Why add all of this? It's just extra complication, and doesn't add anything except a middle finger to cross-over games. I'd keep the bit about vampires and similar granting angst because it's thematic - might even expand on it - but the rest should really be dropped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">When the Monitor uses any Arcanos on a wraith, the player may spend 2 additional<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Pathos to apply that Arcanos' effects to one of the target's Fetters. Alternately, she may apply the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Arcanos to a location or object that is the focus of the target's Legacy or Memoriam background.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Alternately, when the Monitor uses any Arcanos on a Fetter or a focus of Legacy or Memoriam,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">the player may spend 2 additional Pathos to instead apply that Arcanos' effects directly to the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">wraith in question</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Are the first two uses applying instead of or in addition to applying to the target Wraith?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, on a final note, I think it might be best to consider structuring powers a little differently. I might put the roll and costs separately from the main body of the text when possible, so they are easily found when quick-referencing. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T22:56:40-08:00","id":354503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">\u2022\u2022 Echoes in the Web (Ancient)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Once the Monitor learns to perceive the energy traces that bind the Restless to their Fetters, she</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">can refine this sense to uncover more subtle relationships between the wraith and the world of</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">the Quick. Movement in the Web reveals the emotional resonance between a given wraith and</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">the collective minds of humanity.</span></span> </div> </div> </div> In the second to last line should not &quot;Movement in the Web&quot; be &quot;Echoes in the Web&quot; as per the name of the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4574-laughing-lord","name":"Laughing Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T00:59:17-08:00","id":354546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/354396-lifeweb-review-critique#post354396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The Monitor can use this art on a living (or undead) supernatural being, but doing so requires an<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">additional Pathos expenditure equal to the subject's Willpower. The subject also must spend 5<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">points of whatever supernatural energy it uses in lieu of Pathos (e.g., Blood, Rage, Quintessence,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">and if all else fails, Willpower). Using Souls Interwoven on a vampire or other undead creature<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">also gives the Monitor's Shadow an amount of temporary Angst equal to half the deathless thing's<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Willpower</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></i></span><i>.</i> </div> </div> </div>Why add all of this? It's just extra complication, and doesn't add anything except a middle finger to cross-over games. I'd keep the bit about vampires and similar granting angst because it's thematic - might even expand on it - but the rest should really be dropped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd want to add my voice to the choir in questioning this. Why the exorbitant extra cost? And why does being undead cause extra Angst, again considerable amount, to be gained? Why would it be more Angst generating to bind myself with a Humanity 8+ saint who rarely if ever even has selfish thoughts, just look at the ridiculous demands of high humanity, than it would be to bind myself to a normal mortal serial killer who likes to torture his victims before killing them, almost ensuring all the victims go either straight to Oblivion or if they stay behind they do so as Specters?<br /> <br /> Just do not get the extra costs here, other than to screw over crossover games that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cannot readily understand the difference between &quot;surveying&quot; and &quot;assessing&quot; a location. You might want to clarify. </div> </div> </div>I too cannot really see the difference in here so some clarity would be nice.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I am so happy to finally get more material on the Monitors as they sadly never had their own Guildbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:13:25-08:00","id":354975,"title":"","content":"Based on the verbs used and the definition of said verbs:<br /> <br /> Survey would be the idea of Examining and recording the area and feature of where the Fetter is: Essentially figuring out the borders and location.<br /> <br /> Assess would be the idea of evaluating or estimating the value/nature/Ability/quaility of the fetter's location.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:05:02-08:00","id":355162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/354396-lifeweb-review-critique?p=354546#post354546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd want to add my voice to the choir in questioning this. Why the exorbitant extra cost? And why does being undead cause extra Angst, again considerable amount, to be gained? Why would it be more Angst generating to bind myself with a Humanity 8+ saint who rarely if ever even has selfish thoughts, just look at the ridiculous demands of high humanity, than it would be to bind myself to a normal mortal serial killer who likes to torture his victims before killing them, almost ensuring all the victims go either straight to Oblivion or if they stay behind they do so as Specters?<br /> <br /> Just do not get the extra costs here, other than to screw over crossover games that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Angst cost for vampires (and potentially other creatures) make sense because anything that is associated with death, destruction or decay is typically tied to Oblivion, and invoking the forces of Oblivion leads to a rise in Angst. Vampires cause angst because of their representation of death - even the nicest vampire is as dead as an iron nail. So by willingly embracing such a symbol of death, it's understandable to pick up some Angst. It also works gamewise to counterbalance an extremely hard to destroy Fetter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneyard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the verbs used and the definition of said verbs:<br /> <br /> Survey would be the idea of Examining and recording the area and feature of where the Fetter is: Essentially figuring out the borders and location.<br /> <br /> Assess would be the idea of evaluating or estimating the value/nature/Ability/quality of the fetter's location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading it, one is based on Alertness and one is based on Awareness, which is the more supernatural of the two abilities. Looking at it, I can't see a good reason for the cost differential right off hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T16:09:46-08:00","id":355200,"title":"","content":"It could do with clarification, but I take it to mean that the character must spend Pathos in order to apply her Awareness to the fetter's location (and thus gain mystical impressions, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1562-fikealox","name":"Fikealox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:53:19-08:00","id":356167,"title":"","content":"I can see that's the case, but I don't see why it's necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T22:26:32-08:00","id":356275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Angst cost for vampires (and potentially other creatures) make sense because anything that is associated with death, destruction or decay is typically tied to Oblivion, and invoking the forces of Oblivion leads to a rise in Angst. Vampires cause angst because of their representation of death - even the nicest vampire is as dead as an iron nail. </div> </div> </div>Vampires on the other hand are eternal by nature not decaying or representative of normal death so it's arguable. They are in a larger metaphysical sense Wyrm tainted with a considerable touch of Weaver thrown into the mix but they are not directly Oblivion related unless speaking of certain twisted and fallen creatures. But if the Angst cost is added there for such a justification, and metagamely as a balancing factor for them being more enduring Fetters than most, it should be a set cost instead of dependent upon the Vampire Willpower. Willpower represents resolve, and while a strong willed beings tend to have stronger Shadows as well it isn't by itself something that implies the touch of Oblivion, and as such is one of those things a Psyche uses to oppose the call of Oblivion and the whispers of his Shadow. Better explanation would be that the Vampiric Beast is touched by Oblivion, though again that is somewhat stretching it as the Beast seeks survival above all else where as Shadows apart from a few exception tend to be self destructive actively seeking Oblivion and even those few exceptions tend to wish to survive only to spread their pain to others, but if that is the case then it shouldn't be said to apply to all Undead beings only those infected with a Beast and still the cost being tied to their WP is odd to say the least.<br /> <br /> Also there seems to be no explanation or reason for why it cost so ridiculous amount of Pathos and in addition to that a ridiculously large contribution of the other beings energy as well. At best the cost can be 15 Pathos, 3 Willpower, (5 Angst, but only if Undead, being Nephandi even in service of Oblivion has no such extra cost) + 5 Blood/Rage/Quintessence/Willpower which is ridiculously much considering the effect. Besides why it is Rage for the Garou and Fera? Considering were talking about a merger of souls such spiritual matters would likely be governed by Gnosis rather than Rage.<br /> <br /> To me it just seems needlessly punitive to Crossover games and the Angst cost still seems a bit random as it isn't tied to actual Oblivion taint, which for example the Nephandi have a lot more than most Vampires ever will, but simply the Undead state. So in my personal opinion a more reasonable cost along with either more universal Angst cost, I'd see it being more relevant to living subjects in general rather than supernatural only since tying a living person to a death thing -you- is much more Angst filled moment than tying an Undead being to you, that if not a set number at least would be tied to how Oblivion tainted someone is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:45:52-08:00","id":356855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/354396-lifeweb-review-critique?p=356275#post356275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires on the other hand are eternal by nature not decaying or representative of normal death so it's arguable. They are in a larger metaphysical sense Wyrm tainted with a considerable touch of Weaver thrown into the mix but they are not directly Oblivion related unless speaking of certain twisted and fallen creatures. But if the Angst cost is added there for such a justification, and metagamely as a balancing factor for them being more enduring Fetters than most, it should be a set cost instead of dependent upon the Vampire Willpower. Willpower represents resolve, and while a strong willed beings tend to have stronger Shadows as well it isn't by itself something that implies the touch of Oblivion, and as such is one of those things a Psyche uses to oppose the call of Oblivion and the whispers of his Shadow. Better explanation would be that the Vampiric Beast is touched by Oblivion, though again that is somewhat stretching it as the Beast seeks survival above all else where as Shadows apart from a few exception tend to be self destructive actively seeking Oblivion and even those few exceptions tend to wish to survive only to spread their pain to others, but if that is the case then it shouldn't be said to apply to all Undead beings only those infected with a Beast and still the cost being tied to their WP is odd to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are eternal, in that they are eternally dead, and further cause death, suffering, and corruption wherever they go. The Wyrm/Weaver distinction is meaningless for Wraith. They don't decay physically-well, not exactly-but they do decay spiritually except in a few rare corner cases, but finding a vampire who has achieved Giolconda, let alone binding to one, is probably too much of a rare situation to address in a non-Vampire book.That being said, I agree that it doesn't make in-game sense to tie it to Willpower; that just gives us a good universal trait to use for other such things, such is if I want to introduce say, Curse-style mummies into my CWoD game, or or some homebrew zombie/revenant/golem type thing. Even now I would like to think bonding to say, a fomori would be a good reason for an Angst gain. I hadn't even thought of Nephandi; good point. A flat Angst gain though might be better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also there seems to be no explanation or reason for why it cost so ridiculous amount of Pathos and in addition to that a ridiculously large contribution of the other beings energy as well. At best the cost can be 15 Pathos, 3 Willpower, (5 Angst, but only if Undead, being Nephandi even in service of Oblivion has no such extra cost) + 5 Blood/Rage/Quintessence/Willpower which is ridiculously much considering the effect. Besides why it is Rage for the Garou and Fera? Considering were talking about a merger of souls such spiritual matters would likely be governed by Gnosis rather than Rage. </div> </div> </div>Rage is a closer analog to Angst anyway, not Pathos. It is a ridiculously costly effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me it just seems needlessly punitive to Crossover games and the Angst cost still seems a bit random as it isn't tied to actual Oblivion taint, which for example the Nephandi have a lot more than most Vampires ever will, but simply the Undead state. So in my personal opinion a more reasonable cost along with either more universal Angst cost, I'd see it being more relevant to living subjects in general rather than supernatural only since tying a living person to a death thing -you- is much more Angst filled moment than tying an Undead being to you, that if not a set number at least would be tied to how Oblivion tainted someone is. </div> </div> </div>A universal Angst cost seems more fair, easy to apply, and more stable, certainly. I believe that again, the symbolic nature of tying yourself to an undead creature does say something about you, but I don't see why we couldn't expand the Angst penalty on an ad hoc basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T19:36:05-08:00","id":358744,"title":"","content":"I can sense other wraiths normally already. Having to pay Pathos to tell if other wraiths were present is just weird, and no, it shouldn't be worth a Pathos. If a supernatural presences is threatening a character's Fetters, then I placed it there because I want the characters to go immediately check out that threat. That becomes a potential plot hook, as they go to investigate further. If it's something they have to pay for, then either as a GM never use it, which means they never feel the need to pay for it, or if I do use it, it builds player paranoia and it turns into Pathos tax - an obligation. Obligations aren't fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T22:50:53-08:00","id":366079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assess lets the wraith monitor the area around his Fetter from anywhere. If you want them to go immediately to check out a threat to them, they'll probably become aware of it by this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly the point of the power, but if it costs Pathos to get that information, it fails at that. Information giving powers are there specifically so you can give the players the needed trail of breadcrumbs; if they have to pay for those breadcrumbs it's going to make them less likely to pick up on these things. Again, if I as the ST pull &quot;Yeah, you used the power, but you didn't spend Pathos to see the supernatural bits, so you couldn't do anything until it was too late&quot;, I am going to look like a dick. It's not like they aren't going to have to spend a ton of Pathos if shit IS going down. I don't see a good justification for the added cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}